<h3>Three New Apple Smart Home Products Coming on October 13</h3><br/>
A couple of those leaked products above could be arriving very shortly, as <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman says Apple will be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/30/apple-home-products-coming-on-october-13/">introducing a trio of new smart home products on Tuesday, October 13</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/HomePod-minis-on-gradient-feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067302" /><br/>
Apple will reportedly debut its long-rumored smart home hub product, as well as the new HomePod mini and Apple TV models, and while he didn't specify how Apple will introduce them, signs are <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/30/apple-event-on-october-13/">pointing to some sort of event</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Apple retail stores have reportedly also <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/01/apple-stores-receive-do-not-open-boxes/">received confidential boxes that are marked "Do Not Open Until October 8"</a> and which are likely to contain merchandising materials. It's unclear, however, if they are for the upcoming iPhone Duo launch or something related to the smart home product introduction.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>Apple Smart Home Hub to Feature iMac G4-Style Design</h3><br/>
Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/30/apple-home-hub-imac-g4-style-design/">long-rumored smart home hub will have an iMac G4-style design</a> and a host of unique features, <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman reports.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Home-Hub-Command-Center-with-Dome-Base-Colors-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1068235" /><br/>
The smart home hub is said to feature a square 6-inch display, with variants that can be placed on a countertop or mounted on a wall. It features a single FaceTime camera on the front, with microphones and speakers in its connected base.<br/>
<br/>
Leaks suggest the hub <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/01/apple-home-hub-four-colors-rumored/">may be available in Silver, Space Gray, Starlight, and Rose Pink colors</a>, and will be able to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/30/home-hub-photo-face/">display user-customizable Photo Faces</a> pulled from your photos library, memories, and shared albums, a feature that appears similar to what will be available for StandBy mode on the iPhone Duo.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>iPhone Duo Reportedly Facing Production Problems Ahead of Launch</h3><br/>
The iPhone Duo is reportedly <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/29/iphone-duo-reportedly-facing-production-problems/">facing production difficulties ahead of its October launch</a>, with early output expected to be limited.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-feature.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1068262" /><br/>
A person said to be close to Foxconn's supply chain told China's Jiemian News that final assembly yields for Apple's first foldable iPhone were only slightly above 60% as of September 17. The source said that, under Apple's current quality standards, it could take another six months to a year for the assembly line to reach a mature yield.<br/>
<br/>
According to the source, Foxconn is repeatedly adjusting equipment, assembly processes, and production settings as it makes the iPhone Duo at scale. The source also said suppliers were waiting to see whether Apple would ease any quality requirements to accelerate production.<br/>
